# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .gitignore — ALO English Test Platform
#
# Rule of thumb: the repository contains what a deploy needs, and nothing
# else. The host clones this on every push, so every byte here is a byte the
# build has to fetch before it can start.
#
# If a path is listed here but is also tracked in the index, that is a bug —
# `git ls-files -i -c --exclude-standard` must come back empty except for the
# one deliberate exception noted under "Environment" below.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# ─── Testing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/coverage

# ─── Next.js build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
/.next/
/out/
/build
/dist/

# ─── Environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real environment files are never committed.
#
# DELIBERATE EXCEPTION: the root `.env` IS tracked. It contains non-secret
# defaults only, so a fresh checkout and a host build both boot even when the
# panel is only partly configured. Every production secret is set in the host's
# environment panel, and Next.js never overwrites a value already present in
# process.env — so panel values always win over this file. If you put a real
# secret in `.env`, you have committed it to a public repository.
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# ─── Databases ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provisioned on the host by `prisma migrate deploy`. A database in git means
# dev accounts and a stale migration state shipping to production.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
/db/*
!/db/.gitkeep

# ─── Runtime data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Created on the host at runtime. Must live outside the release directory —
# see APP_DATA_DIR in .env.example.
/upload/*
!/upload/.gitkeep
/download/*
!/download/.gitkeep
/logs/

# ─── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
dev.log
dev.out.log
server.log

# ─── Release archives ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# ─── Legacy sibling projects ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Archived codebases that are not part of this deployment. The CI artifact
# excludes them too (.github/workflows/ci.yml → "Create source archive").
/english-aloeducation/
/tool-results/
/worklog.md

# cpanel-production/ IS deployed: /api/deliverable and /api/deliverables serve
# from it for SUPER_ADMIN. Its build output and logs are not — those routes
# skip both directories when walking the tree.
/cpanel-production/dist/
/cpanel-production/logs/

# ─── Superseded delivery guides ────────────────────────────────────────
# These describe a VPS/nginx/systemd delivery that was retired. The
# authoritative guide is HOSTINGER_DEPLOYMENT.md. They remain in git history.
/FINAL-DELIVERY-GUIDE.md
/PRODUCTION-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md
/FINAL-PRODUCTION-PACKAGE.zip
/english-aloeducation-web-crm-production.tar.gz
/SHA256SUMS.txt

# ─── Tooling / editor / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
local-*
.claude
.z-ai-config
/test
/prompt
/skills/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.pem

# ─── Kept on purpose ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
!mini-services/
!examples/

# Runtime PID files from .zscripts/dev.sh
*.pid

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
